605	     7	#   no environment, no secrets and no OIDC token, and uploads the resolved Build
606	     8	#   Output with a SHA256SUMS whose digest it reports.
607	     9	# - deploy runs in the dev|production environment and mints a short-lived
608	    10	#   Cloudflare token from the token issuer. It checks out only .github/release/,
609	    11	#   verifies the artifact against the digest the build job reported, installs
610	    12	#   the cf CLI pinned in .github/release/cf, and runs only
611	    13	#   .github/release/deploy-legacy.sh or deploy-data.sh. Those treat the artifact
612	    14	#   as data and refuse anything but the pinned targets in
613	    15	#   .github/release/targets/. That is what makes an account-wide token safe: the
614	    16	#   data sync Workflow PUT has no per-Worker permission, so only Dax-reviewed
